From: jahshaka <jahshaka@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clusterlod: a per-group verify hook (clodMesh::verify_group)

CLUSTER-LOCK-3, 2026-09-29. The mesh bake bounds how far a group's
simplification may move the surface: a group at depth d may not move any
level-0 point past kDagLockFactor x ITS OWN error (DAG-LOCK-1). That bound is
a property of ONE group at the moment it is simplified; the only lock input
clusterlod had was clodMesh::vertex_lock, ONE array honoured by every level,
so the bake had to lock a vertex for the whole build and rebuild the whole DAG
(up to 16 builds): a vertex a depth-1 group needed stayed locked up to the
root (uv-sphere-20k root 78 -> 2916 triangles) and the temple's bake went
3.7 -> 8.1 s. (Patch 0001, the per-LEVEL lock of CLUSTER-LOCK-2, was the
parked prototype of the same idea; it never landed and its number is retired.)

The hook: an optional callback on clodMesh, called for every group that
simplified (not stuck), after its simplification and before it is output,
with the group's input indices, its simplified indices and the error it will
be output with. NULL accepts. A lock array re-simplifies THIS group with those
locks added to the level's (boundary, terminal, vertex_lock) locks, and the
result is verified again; the added locks are restored before the next group,
so nothing carries to another group or level. A re-simplification never takes
the sloppy fallback (it snaps every unlocked vertex to a grid and can drop a
locked vertex with its triangles: measured on the bake's scan stand-in, the
retries of a depth-2 group re-offended four times running with the error
doubling each time). One that gets STUCK makes the group terminal exactly as a
stuck first result does (its clusters stay as they are; patch 0002 keeps their
border): a group that cannot simplify within the bound its caller holds it to
is not simplified (measured: a 109-triangle pile of 33 debris islands on the
stand-in). The callback bounds the attempts. Unset keeps upstream's behaviour
exactly. Upstream candidate: two fields on clodMesh and two static helpers.

Applied at configure (irisgl/CMakeLists.txt) to a copy of the vendored header
in the build tree; the vendored file itself is never edited.
---
--- a/clusterlod.h
+++ b/clusterlod.h
@@ -83,6 +83,17 @@
 	// input vertex locks; allows to preserve additional seams (when not using attribute_protect_mask) or lock vertices via meshopt_SimplifyVertex_* flags
 	const unsigned char* vertex_lock;
 
+	// optional verification of every simplified group: called after a group at the given depth has been simplified (and is not
+	// stuck), with the group's input indices, its simplified indices and the error the group will be output with; attempt is 0
+	// for the first result of the group and counts the re-simplifications after it
+	// returns NULL to accept the result, or a lock array (vertex_count entries, same flags as vertex_lock) to re-simplify the group
+	// with these locks added to the ones the group already has; the array must stay valid until the next call
+	// a re-simplification honours the added locks: it never takes the sloppy fallback (which snaps every unlocked vertex to a grid
+	// and can drop a locked vertex with its triangles); one that gets stuck makes the group terminal, like a stuck first result
+	// the callback bounds the number of attempts (it must eventually return NULL)
+	const unsigned char* (*verify_group)(void* context, int depth, int attempt, const unsigned int* group_indices, size_t group_index_count, const unsigned int* simplified_indices, size_t simplified_index_count, float error);
+	void* verify_group_context;
+
 	// attribute weights for attribute-aware simplification; maps to meshopt_simplifyWithAttributes parameters
 	const float* attribute_weights;
 	size_t attribute_count;
@@ -518,6 +529,47 @@
 	return lod;
 }
 
+static float groupError(const clodConfig& config, float merged_error, float error)
+{
+	return std::max(merged_error * config.simplify_error_merge_previous, error) + error * config.simplify_error_merge_additive;
+}
+
+static void verifyGroup(const clodConfig& config, const clodMesh& mesh, const std::vector<unsigned int>& merged, std::vector<unsigned char>& locks, size_t target_size, float merged_error, int depth, std::vector<unsigned int>& simplified, float& error)
+{
+	// locks added for this group only; restored before the next group is simplified
+	std::vector<std::pair<unsigned int, unsigned char> > saved;
+
+	// the sloppy fallback ignores the locks' purpose (it snaps unlocked vertices to a grid and may drop a locked one), so a
+	// re-simplification only uses the attribute-aware simplifier
+	clodConfig retry_config = config;
+	retry_config.simplify_fallback_sloppy = false;
+
+	for (int attempt = 0;; ++attempt)
+	{
+		const unsigned char* extra = mesh.verify_group(mesh.verify_group_context, depth, attempt, &merged[0], merged.size(), simplified.data(), simplified.size(), groupError(config, merged_error, error));
+		if (!extra)
+			break;
+
+		for (size_t k = 0; k < merged.size(); ++k)
+		{
+			unsigned int v = merged[k];
+
+			if (extra[v] & ~locks[v])
+			{
+				saved.push_back(std::make_pair(v, locks[v]));
+				locks[v] |= extra[v];
+			}
+		}
+
+		simplified = simplify(retry_config, mesh, merged, locks, target_size, &error);
+		if (simplified.size() > merged.size() * config.simplify_threshold)
+			break; // the added locks got the group stuck; the caller makes it terminal
+	}
+
+	for (size_t k = saved.size(); k > 0; --k)
+		locks[saved[k - 1].first] = saved[k - 1].second;
+}
+
 static int outputGroup(const clodConfig& config, const clodMesh& mesh, const std::vector<Cluster>& clusters, const std::vector<int>& group, const clodBounds& simplified, int depth, void* output_context, clodOutput output_callback)
 {
 	std::vector<clodCluster> group_clusters(group.size());
@@ -673,6 +725,11 @@
 
 			float error = 0.f;
 			std::vector<unsigned int> simplified = simplify(config, mesh, merged, locks, target_size, &error);
+
+			// let the caller verify the simplified group; it may re-simplify it with more locks (and get it stuck)
+			if (mesh.verify_group && simplified.size() <= merged.size() * config.simplify_threshold)
